WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.946
AI systems are not only models.

2
00:00:01.946 --> 00:00:13.669
They may include prompts, tools, retrieval systems, vector databases, memory, APIs, plugins, user interfaces, logs, and business workflows.

3
00:00:13.669 --> 00:00:16.882
Red teaming must consider how these pieces interact.

4
00:00:16.882 --> 00:00:30.033
A model response that seems harmless in isolation may become risky when connected to a tool that sends email, modifies tickets, accesses files, retrieves information, or influences a business decision.

5
00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:31.629
Outputs alone are not enough.

6
00:00:31.629 --> 00:00:43.473
Assessors should ask what input shaped the output, what data the system used, what tool or workflow could be triggered, what permissions apply, and what human review or monitoring exists.

7
00:00:43.473 --> 00:00:46.317
This whole-system view keeps the assessment practical.

8
00:00:46.317 --> 00:00:57.980
It helps teams understand whether risk comes from the model, application logic, integration design, data handling, authorization, oversight, or a combination of those factors.
